It was assumed that the amorphous content was mainly comprised by reactive silica. To ensure the concrete mixtures are informed by this XRF and XRD analysis, the implied % of amorphous silica of all (amorphous + crystalline) contents were calculated as [100 * 33.8%/(84.9%) =] 39.81%. Subsequently, by applying this ratio to the XRF total, the calculated amorphous silica percentage is [(83.13% * 39.81%) =] 33% [ 30 ,  31 ]. Practically, not all the assumed amorphous content will completely react therefore lower reactive silica percentages of 30%, 25% and 20% were selected to trail different mixtures. Furthermore, the modified AA formulation presumed complete derivation of Na 2 O from the NaOH solution. Finally, the SCBA/NaOH ratio was calculated and later approximated to its first decimal place, to assess and ease the mixture usability. The required SCBA for each mixture was calculated using Eq. ( 3 ). 1 M + = Na 2 O flyash + GGBS M + = 7.5 % \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
